{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 9, :comments ["<b>Myrrh</b> — There is a dispute concerning the word מר. Those who say that אהלות [aloes] found with sea fish is not correct, for it is written: כאהלים נטע ה׳ [like tents has YHWH planted]." "And some say: that also קציעות [cassia] is a species that has a good fragrance, and it is the way of the sacred tongue to say: אדם פטדה וברקת [carnelian, jasper, and emerald], the vav being with the last or without a vav, like: אדם שת אנוש [Adam, Seth, Enosh]. If so, it should have been מר אהלות קציעות, or מר אהלות וקציעות. Perhaps this word [קציעות] comes by a strange path. But the correct view is that קציעות is from the root מקצועות [cuttings], and the word is in construct state to בגדותיך [your garments]. And the reason the accent of בגדותיך joins with היכלי שן [ivory palaces], is because there they are kept in chests." "And the meaning of כי ה' מוציאות [when you are brought forth] from היכלי שן, and the word אשר is lacking, as though it is מהיכלי שן מאשר [from ivory palaces, from where] they rejoiced, or they returned from ivory palaces, for from there they were brought." "And one who says that מני is a name of a nation or a land is not correct, because שן is pointed with kamatz katan [gadol], like every word in the accent [system] that is not in construct state to another."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 45, :notes {0 "Ibn Ezra refutes one opinion by citing an unrelated verse where אהלים means 'tents'; the logic is compressed and no connective explanation is added.", 1 "Ibn Ezra quotes the minimal pairs without explicit connective; the grammar point about vav and lists is compressed.", 2 "The argument is extremely compressed; the text may involve a haplographic omission. Translated hyper-literally.", 3 "Reading קמץ קטן in the source text as kamatz gadol based on Ibn Ezra's standard terminology; the argument concerns why שן cannot be in construct chain, proving מני is not a place name."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:31:01.899280666Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}